<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?LinkID=208121.

     macOS, Apple silicon. There is no osx-x64 profile on purpose: an Intel Mac runs this
     one under Rosetta at a cost the renderer cannot afford, and every Mac that can play
     the game at frame rate is arm64.

     What this produces is not a folder of files but publishmac/GK3Reborn.app - the
     shipping shape on a Mac, and what build/package-macos.sh wraps into an installer
     package. PublishDir points straight into Contents/MacOS so that the executable and
     the libs/<rid> tree land there without being moved afterwards; AppContext.BaseDirectory
     is then Contents/MacOS, which is what every path the game derives is relative to.
     RebornWriteMacAppBundle in GK3Reborn.Host.csproj adds Info.plist, PkgInfo and the icon.

     Publishing from Windows or Linux is fine and gives a complete bundle. It cannot give a
     signed one, and macOS on Apple silicon refuses to run an unsigned executable at all -
     build/package-macos.sh signs it, at minimum ad hoc, as its first step.

     Vulkan on macOS is MoltenVK. The game finds it either from a Vulkan SDK installed on
     the machine or from libMoltenVK.dylib dropped into libs/osx-arm64, which is what
     Silk.NET's resolver is taught about by NativeLibraryLocator - see README, "Running on
     macOS". -->
<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <Configuration>Release</Configuration>
    <Platform>Any CPU</Platform>
    <PublishProtocol>FileSystem</PublishProtocol>
    <_TargetId>Folder</_TargetId>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <RuntimeIdentifier>osx-arm64</RuntimeIdentifier>
    <!-- Overrides the x64 that Directory.Build.props sets for every project: the SDK
         refuses a publish whose PlatformTarget and RuntimeIdentifier disagree, with
         NETSDK1032, rather than letting the RID decide. The profile is imported after the
         props, which is why the override can live here at all. -->
    <PlatformTarget>arm64</PlatformTarget>
    <SelfContained>false</SelfContained>
    <PublishSingleFile>true</PublishSingleFile>

    <RebornMacAppBundle>true</RebornMacAppBundle>
    <RebornMacBundleRoot>publishmac\GK3Reborn.app\</RebornMacBundleRoot>
    <PublishDir>$(RebornMacBundleRoot)Contents\MacOS\</PublishDir>

    <!-- The same three as the Windows profile, and for the same reasons: native libraries
         stay real files under libs/<rid> so that AppContext.BaseDirectory keeps pointing at
         the install root, symbols travel inside the executable, and neither XML docs nor a
         referenced project's .pdb belongs in a shipped bundle. -->
    <IncludeNativeLibrariesForSelfExtract>false</IncludeNativeLibrariesForSelfExtract>
    <DebugType>embedded</DebugType>
    <PublishDocumentationFile>false</PublishDocumentationFile>
    <PublishReferencesDocumentationFiles>false</PublishReferencesDocumentationFiles>
    <AllowedReferenceRelatedFileExtensions>none</AllowedReferenceRelatedFileExtensions>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
